ct in a three-quarter body view, allowing the armor, stance, and surrounding Roman environment to be clearly visible.Style the subject as a Roman warrior, general, or noble figure, wearing ornate epic Roman armor that feels sculpted and organic, as if it was forged specifically for them.The armor should appear cinematic, mythic, and heroic, inspired by ancient Roman design but elevated to the scale of a blockbuster historical epic.Typical armor characteristics may include: • sculpted metal surfaces that follow the contours of the body • engraved patterns inspired by Roman mythology • layered metal and leather elements integrated into the design • intricate ornamental details and symbolic engravings • subtle battle-worn textures and aged materials Do not include any cape or cloak. The armor should stand on its own without a red cape or flowing fabric.The armor should feel slightly organic and artistic rather than rigid, with elegant curves, sculptural shapes, and intricate detailing that make it appear legendary and powerful.Hair and grooming should remain recognizable from the original image while being adapted to fit the historical setting.The subject should have a serious, focused, and inspirational expression, conveying strength, resolve, and leadership. Their face should appear calm, determined, and heroic, as if they are preparing for battle or inspiring those around them.Place the subject in a grand Roman environment, such as: • a massive Roman battlefield at dawn• the steps of an ancient Roman temple• the Roman Colosseum in the background • a dramatic imperial cityscape with marble columns and statues. The environment should feel large, epic, and cinematic, with atmospheric depth, dust or smoke in the air, and distant figures or architecture reinforcing the scale.Lighting should feel dramatic and cinematic, similar to a modern historical epic film, with warm sunlight cutting through dust or clouds, creating strong highlights and deep shadows. Render the image